2026-09-27T09:27:29.6209557Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6210041Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6210502Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6211673Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6213020Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6213145Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6213422Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6213828Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6214459Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6214597Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6214908Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6215083Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6215310Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6215855Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6216187Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6216368Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6216801Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6217060Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6217256Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6217832Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6218352Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6219333Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6220184Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6220382Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6221102Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6221959Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6222438Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6222951Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6223656Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6223793Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6224284Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6224465Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6226702Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6229000Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6229365Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6317358Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6318709Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6319697Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6320540Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6321199Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6321791Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6321952Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6322306Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6322524Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6324352Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6326094Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6327061Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6328440Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:29.6328752Z 
